Original commit body from 05863dd566a771d87bce06f063b8c993e0e1cc23:

The route-parity corpus held five one-per-language cases and gated route-marker
identity with ONE aggregate test over go/java/javascript. Eleven of the thirteen
route-marker producers were therefore never measured, and the three that were
got checked on three properties out of four -- which is how PR #64 was able to
report go clean while go's fifth minting site was violating two of them.

Adds ten fixture cases (django, starlette, go-mount, ruby, php, elixir, swift,
grpc, play-routes, js-named, annotation) and replaces the aggregate with four
per-case property tests, each with its own strict-xfail hole set so the producer
sweep drains one measured number at a time:

  id kind-slot     == Symbol.kind, registered kind (ADR-0036 R2)  --  9 holes
  id name-slot     == sanitize_id_name_segment(Symbol.name) (R1)  --  3 holes
  canonical id     5 anchored segments, {start}-{end} span slot   --  3 holes
  origin provenance non-empty registered origin + a real run id   --  1 hole

A fifth test asserts each analyzer/linker-direct case actually mints a marker,
so none of the above can pass vacuously if a producer regresses. Every hole was
MEASURED by running the full pipeline over the fixtures, not inferred from
reading the producers.

Three of the holes are defects no existing gate could see:

  * go.py's chi/gorilla r.Mount() site was missed by the PR #64 migration and
    violates BOTH slots (route_mount kind-slot fossil, name=handler_ref against
    a "MOUNT {prefix}" name-slot). Invisible because the go fixture is net/http
    only and never exercised a mount. The changelog entry for #64 is corrected
    in place rather than left standing.
  * The Django CBV expander concatenates the colon-bearing name "django:{view}"
    straight into make_symbol_id, emitting a SIX-segment id -- a hard ADR-0036
    grammar break, strictly worse than a wrong slot. Split out as WI-javag.
  * elixir route markers carry an EMPTY Symbol.origin. WI-tufil's check iterated
    origin and so passed vacuously on the empty list -- the "missing provenance"
    half of WI-zugob's own title, hidden by the same mechanism it describes.

Fixtures are now staged to a temp dir before analysis instead of being analyzed
in place. Under tests/fixtures/ the pipeline's own test-path heuristics suppress
the grpc linker outright (byte-identical .proto: 4 markers at an ordinary path,
0 under the fixture path), so an in-place grpc case would have measured the
suppression rather than the producer and passed green.

Two related route-detection defects found while building the fixtures are filed,
not fixed here: php silently drops double-quoted route paths (WI-fadip, the arg
walk accepts tree-sitter `string` but not `encapsed_string`), and grpc mints a
bare line number in its span slot.

No producer changes -- this is the gate, landed before the sweep.

Test module cost rises from 5 to 15 full-pipeline runs (~6 min under coverage
instrumentation, 22s without); that is the price of measuring the fleet rather
than a third of it.

